    <bpmn:process id="W_W3503" name="W3503. Import Ocean Freight, Forwarder &amp; NVOCC Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import PO (links to VS-02.2); ~400–600 TEUs/month
Frequency: Per shipment + continuous
Volume: ~400–600 TEUs/month, ~40% of COGS import
Owner: Logistics / Import
Participants: Logistics (links to VS-06/VS-02.2), Import/Customs (links to VS-87), Procurement (links to VS-03), Freight Forwarder/NVOCC, Shipping Line, Customs Broker (links to VS-87)
Source: workflow W3503 — Import Ocean Freight, Forwarder &amp; NVOCC Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3503_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3503_Lane1" name="Logistics">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3503_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3503_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3503_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3503_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3503_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3503_Start3" name="Import PO (links to VS-02.2); ~400–600 TEUs/month">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3503_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3503_Task4" name="Logistics/Procurement manage the ocean-freight program: shipping-line contracts…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Logistics/Procurement manage the ocean-freight program: shipping-line contracts (FCL) and NVOCC/forwarder relationships (LCL), port-pair lanes (China/Taiwan/Indonesia/Malaysia/Japan/Europe → Manila/Cebu/CDO), BAF/rate negotiation, space allocation in peak season, and carrier performance; integrate to the import plan (links to VS-02.2/W1422 forward-buy)
Responsible (R): Logistics / Procurement
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per contract + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3503_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3503_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3503_Task5" name="Logistics/Forwarder manage the import shipment lifecycle: booking…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Logistics/Forwarder manage the import shipment lifecycle: booking, BL/telex-release, container stuffing/origin, ocean transit, arrival notice, drayage to DC (links to VS-04/W222 yard), and customs clearance (links to VS-87/W2560); track in-transit (W3508) and manage demurrage/detention (W3509/W249)
Responsible (R): Logistics / Forwarder / Customs Broker
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Per shipment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3503_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3503_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3503_Task6" name="Logistics/Finance capture the import landed-cost components (ocean freight…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Logistics/Finance capture the import landed-cost components (ocean freight, BAF, THC, drayage, duty, customs broker, insurance links to VS-87/W3515) to the PO/item for inventory valuation (links to VS-17/W275), reconcile the forwarder invoice (W3513), and report import-freight cost and transit performance (W3512)
Responsible (R): Logistics / Finance
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager / CFO
Duration: Per shipment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3503_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3503_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3503_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3503_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3503_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-559 (ensure controlled execution — Freight Sourcing, Carrier Contracting &amp; Rate Management (PA-110.1).) | - operational: contracts and forward-booking (links to W1422); operational: drayage planning (W3509/W249)
Owner: Logistics / Import</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
